{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming","id":886143,"title":"[2E] Adamant Hand is Underwhelming?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-09T06:02:28-07:00","id":886143,"title":"[2E] Adamant Hand is Underwhelming?","content":"I dunno if it's just me but I'm amazingly underwhelmed by this merit versus the other Order specific merits<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening 2E pg 99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adamant Hand (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Adamantine Arrow Status \u2022, (Athletics, Brawl, or Weaponry \u2022\u2022\u2022, Special)]When taking this Merit, choose Athletics, Weaponry, or Brawl, which your character must have three or more dots in. This Merit allows use of that Skill in combat as a reflexive Order tool Yantra, adding dice to a spell cast on subsequent turns, or to a spell cast reflexively in the same turn as the combat action. You may purchase this Merit multiple times to reflect the other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compared to, say, the Silver Ladder merit<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening 2E pg 102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lex Magica (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisites: Silver Ladder Status \u2022<br /> First, add her Silver Ladder Status or Consilium Status (whichever she\u2019s acting with) to her Doors when a character attempts to outmaneuver her socially (see p. 215).<br /> Second, characters cannot use Willpower to increase dice pools on Social actions or magic which would influence her behavior. Lastly, your character may use her Silver Ladder Status or Consilium Status (whichever is higher) as a Yantra in spells directly enforcing the Lex Magica\u2019s laws. This includes spells to investigate potential crimes, to pursue offenders, to use the law to defend innocence, and any other spell to help the rule of law work more thoroughly. The dice bonus for the Yantra is half the Merit dots used, rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3403-corginaut","name":"Corginaut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:09:07-07:00","id":886146,"title":"","content":"Casting a spell with a yantra bonus in the same turn as doing a combat action is pretty potent - it's essentially an extra action. Breaking the action economy in 2e is pretty rare. Admittedly an Order Tool Yantra is only worth one die, which is also my issue with the Free Council Techne merit - it's a two-dot merit that's slightly worse than the one-dot version of Shadow Name. I really like the flavor of incorporating Sleepers into your castings, but access to two one-die yantras that take up two separate yantra slots is strictly worse than spending two merit dots on one yantra that gives two dice and takes up one yantra slot (to compare the two-dot version of Shadow Name to two dots of Techne). The bonus Withstand rating cloaking your mundane ties is also better than an 8-again that requires everyone else involved in the casting to also have the merit, considering extra successes on spellcasting don't do anything aside from get you closer to an Exceptional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 05-09-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:19:08-07:00","id":886154,"title":"","content":"Does it give a reflexive spell? I'm reading it as &quot;or to a spell cast reflexively in the same turn as the combat action.&quot; I.E it's giving that +1 Yantra bonus reflexively to the spell cast on the next turn or adding +1 Yantra to a spell that you can cast reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3403-corginaut","name":"Corginaut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:37:38-07:00","id":886165,"title":"","content":"I thought it made the combat action reflexive, while the spell takes up your primary action.<br /> <br /> I might be reading it wrong, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:44:48-07:00","id":886169,"title":"","content":"The merit allows for a combat skill use to be an Order Tool Yantra on spells cast in future turns within that combat or a spell you cast reflexively (such as Turn Momentum with the first Reach effect). The merit does not give you a way to make spells reflexive. I'll grant that the comma usage makes this a little confusing.<br /> <br /> A merit that allows you to break the &quot;one action a turn&quot; rule with ANY spell would be insanely powerful, especially when making the way you get the additional action to cast a spell. . .you know, being part of the Order of Let's Fight People and attacking someone. I could MAYBE see some subsequent merit letting you do so, but it would need some STEEP pre-requisites. I'm talking high Gnosis, multiple fighting style dots, and even then giving you the ability to spend a Reach (maybe TWO) in order to reflexively cast a spell as part of an attack. MAYBE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:47:56-07:00","id":886176,"title":"","content":"Throwing an Aimed Spell is a combat action using Athletics Skill. You can pretty much trigger this every round, which gives you two reflexive yantras to your spells - in combat, this is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:07:24-07:00","id":886191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886176#post886176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throwing an Aimed Spell is a combat action using Athletics Skill. You can pretty much trigger this every round, which gives you two reflexive yantras to your spells - in combat, this is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is an excellent idea and I hadn't thought of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:08:21-07:00","id":886193,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm reading it as adding the skill (the dots) as a Yantra, meaning it won't be +1, but +dots, with the downside that it's only usable every other round (barring reflexive spells).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:12:57-07:00","id":886200,"title":"","content":"It counts as an Order Tool, and Tools all add +1 die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:15:50-07:00","id":886204,"title":"","content":"It's probably just +1. It says that &quot;using the skill&quot; is considered &quot;a reflexive order tool yantra&quot;. Order Yantras are fixed at +1. In practice, it's a free +1, because in combat you would be insane to use non reflexive Yantras. It's not very strong, it would be probably better if the tool was also considered dedicated. With &quot;Skill dots in Yantra bonus&quot;, it would be broken as fuck; you would pick the Athletics as Adamant Hand style, pick a Athletics Rote in your spell, and pick 5 skill points into Athletics. +10 Yantra bonus choo choo train.<br /> EDIT<br /> Of course, current spelling makes it sound like you can get multiple instances of this going, because it's subsequent turns and spells, not next turn and next spell. So in turn 1, cast Aimed Spell using Athletics. You get 1 Reflexive Order Yantra. In turn 2. cast Aimed Spell using Athletics. You benefit from one free reflexive +1 yantra. Turn 3, cast Aimed Spell using Athletics, you benefit from two reflexive +1 yantras (so 3 reflexive yantras in total). This interpretation makes it actually good without being brokkkkkkkkken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:52:59-07:00","id":886248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886176#post886176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throwing an Aimed Spell is a combat action using Athletics Skill. You can pretty much trigger this every round, which gives you two reflexive yantras to your spells - in combat, this is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately the aim roll comes after you've cast, so.. No.<br /> <br /> The main use of Hand is that where every other mage has to stop fighting and rely on their normal Defense while casting spells that take more than one turn, an Arrow can fight and Dodge all she likes - and even use them as yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:54:26-07:00","id":886252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886248#post886248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unfortunately the aim roll comes after you've cast, so.. No.<br /> <br /> The main use of Hand is that where every other mage has to stop fighting and rely on their normal Defense while casting spells that take more than one turn, an Arrow can fight and Dodge all she likes - and even use them as yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But couldn't you use the aim roll as a Yantra for the NEXT spell you cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:57:53-07:00","id":886254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886248#post886248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main use of Hand is that where every other mage has to stop fighting and rely on their normal Defense while casting spells that take more than one turn, an Arrow can fight and Dodge all she likes - and even use them as yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our group has been in ~5 fights, and I don't think I have ever seen a Mage take an action other then spellcasting during a fight (well, one surrender action, but I wouldn't count that). I know we have less combat/session than most, but is my group also atypical for not using mundane combat actions during fights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:58:10-07:00","id":886256,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was talking about next spell. So you go Cast-Aim-Fire!, and in next round, you get +1 for the trouble. It's amazing, because +1 in combat context *is* amazing.<br /> Merit mentions subsequent turns - what if I spend 3 rounds hacking away with my Adamant Hand, and on the 4th round, I go cast? Is that one Yantra, or one-per-combat action? That would be also neat for Magical Samurai Wrestlers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886254#post886254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our group has been in ~5 fights, and I don't think I have ever seen a Mage take an action other then spellcasting during a fight (well, one surrender action, but I wouldn't count that). I know we have less combat/session than most, but is my group also atypical for not using mundane combat actions during fights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of people don't do non spellcasting actions because they are weaker than spellcasting. This merit gives you an excuse to whack a dude with a sword and then feel rewarded for doing so when you follow up with a spellcast. It's a concept enabler and a carrot to not spend all combat casting spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-09-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:30:36-07:00","id":886294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886254#post886254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our group has been in ~5 fights, and I don't think I have ever seen a Mage take an action other then spellcasting during a fight (well, one surrender action, but I wouldn't count that). I know we have less combat/session than most, but is my group also atypical for not using mundane combat actions during fights?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think most Mages are by far better at fighting with Magic than fighting with physical attacks because two dots in Weaponry, a specialty, and four dots in a fighting style could instead be a Gnosis and an Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:36:48-07:00","id":886297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886294#post886294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think most Mages are by far better at fighting with Magic than fighting with physical attacks because two dots in Weaponry, a specialty, and four dots in a fighting style could instead be a Gnosis and an Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the other hand, a single dot in Firearms can be bought at character creation (so it doesn't compete with Gnosis and Arcana) and allows you a nice versatility. Though yes, in many cases, a Fraying spell is infintiely better at doing damage than any mundane means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:30:34-07:00","id":886404,"title":"","content":"Also true, though aside from some corner cases I think most Mages would still be wildly better off casting Magic in combat -- not necessarily to kill, but from the sheer amount of options that let you NOT kill someone.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm a big fan of a single dot of Firearms just from a &quot;I'm getting into some shit and went to the range a few times with my new gun because I'm actually kinda scared&quot; angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:36:11-07:00","id":886411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886404#post886404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also true, though aside from some corner cases I think most Mages would still be wildly better off casting Magic in combat -- not necessarily to kill, but from the sheer amount of options that let you NOT kill someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that in order to succeed with many spells, at least with decent factors, you need to employ as many Yantras as possible, and that takes time and attention. A lot of typical mage adversaries will gut a mage before he utters a syllable in High Speech, no less finishes a combat spell. Adamant Hand allows a mage to Dodge attacks or even go on offensive while still employing a Yantra in combat. Not only is this beneficial for the mage with the AH merit, it could buy time for his less martially-inclined cabalmates to employ their Yantras in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:27:04-07:00","id":886491,"title":"","content":"I feel like the only time you're really needing a bunch of spell factors is for direct-damage spells, which are typically pretty bad (if rad as all hell). A starting Moros can reliably turn five guns into a puddle as an instant action with a rather good chance of success and a 1 in 10 chance of Paradox. I feel like that's incredibly effective and that spell wouldn't even require penalties for spell factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:58:20-07:00","id":886522,"title":"","content":"People with guns aren't a Mage's worst problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:03:57-07:00","id":886531,"title":"","content":"1/10 chance after adding the sleeper dox dice? That seems like more mana than I would want to spend.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, I believe it is far safer for a wizard to avoid combat, or use sniping and ambush techniques if he's going to rely purely on casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:29:29-07:00","id":886551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886522#post886522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People with guns aren't a Mage's worst problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mage's worst problems aren't fights involving initiative anyway, and yet that's what we're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886531#post886531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1/10 chance after adding the sleeper dox dice? That seems like more mana than I would want to spend.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, I believe it is far safer for a wizard to avoid combat, or use sniping and ambush techniques if he's going to rely purely on casting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Using a dedicated magical tool nets you -2 Paradox Dice. +2 for the Reach beyond the free one, +1 for the Sleepers, -2 for the Tool, -1 for a Mana. And there being 5 of them doesn't even add any dice-tricks since it's a chance die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:52:31-07:00","id":886647,"title":"","content":"Dude, Mind Shield practically automatically deals with uppity sleepers.<br /> <br /> Can I see some example of Adamantine Hand working as intended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:24:32-07:00","id":886671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886647#post886647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, Mind Shield practically automatically deals with uppity sleepers.<br /> <br /> Can I see some example of Adamantine Hand working as intended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably Dodging (Although I'd disagree with this because it's a stat derived from Athletics and not an athletics roll (Since dodge is defense doubled)<br /> So you're taking an athletics, brawl, firearms or weaponry attack roll this turn to add +1 reflexively to next turns spell (which would have another +yantra that can be used reflexively when you cast)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3403-corginaut","name":"Corginaut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:32:24-07:00","id":886678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corginaut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886671#post886671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably Dodging (Although I'd disagree with this because it's a stat derived from Athletics and not an athletics roll (Since dodge is defense doubled)<br /> So you're taking an athletics, brawl, firearms or weaponry attack roll this turn to add +1 reflexively to next turns spell (which would have another +yantra that can be used reflexively when you cast)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Adamantine Hand does not cover Firearms, only Brawl, Weaponry and Athletics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:42:19-07:00","id":886685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886678#post886678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Adamantine Hand does not cover Firearms, only Brawl, Weaponry and Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Heh. I didn't consult my post before posting. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3403-corginaut","name":"Corginaut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:46:02-07:00","id":886686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corginaut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886685#post886685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Heh. I didn't consult my post before posting. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dave mentioned during open development that he was considering including Firearms in Adamantine Hand, but he obviously decided against it.<br /> <br /> If people wanted to include AH (Firearms) as a house rule, it probably wouldn't be the end of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:48:54-07:00","id":886746,"title":"","content":"A Thyrsus that uses Adsmant Hand to buff themselves up every time they throw a punch is one hell of a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:52:07-07:00","id":886749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886746#post886746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Thyrsus that uses Adsmant Hand to buff themselves up every time they throw a punch is one hell of a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The buff isn't reflexive though (I think) so it'd be<br /> Turn 1: Punch (+1 Yantra)<br /> Turn 2: Honing the Form<br /> Turn 3: Punch (+1 Yantra)<br /> Turn 4: Body Control<br /> etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3403-corginaut","name":"Corginaut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:59:32-07:00","id":886755,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Question is, can you go:<br /> Turn 1: Punch (+1 Yantra)<br /> Turn 2: Punch (+2 Yantras)<br /> Turn 3: Punch (+3 Yantras)<br /> Turn 4: Spell (bank in three +1 Yantras as COMBO FINISHER)<br /> That would make people with Persona and this merit very good at combat casting in a fun way that requires an action setup. Which is always fun for gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:14:22-07:00","id":886770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886755#post886755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Question is, can you go:<br /> Turn 1: Punch (+1 Yantra)<br /> Turn 2: Punch (+2 Yantras)<br /> Turn 3: Punch (+3 Yantras)<br /> Turn 4: Spell (bank in three +1 Yantras as COMBO FINISHER)<br /> That would make people with Persona and this merit very good at combat casting in a fun way that requires an action setup. Which is always fun for gameplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ld4It2O5XHA?t=2m16s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ld4It2O5XHA?t=2m16s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ld4It2O5XHA?t=2m16s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Ld4It2O5XHA?t=2m16s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:39:04-07:00","id":886794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886522#post886522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People with guns aren't a Mage's worst problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best way to use a gun? Aim it at a dude as a Yantra, make them think you are going to put some bullets in them so they reflexively grab kinetic/physical Mage Armor, shoot aimed Fast Spell at them :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:42:49-07:00","id":886796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886755#post886755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Question is, can you go:<br /> Turn 1: Punch (+1 Yantra)<br /> Turn 2: Punch (+2 Yantras)<br /> Turn 3: Punch (+3 Yantras)<br /> Turn 4: Spell (bank in three +1 Yantras as COMBO FINISHER)<br /> That would make people with Persona and this merit very good at combat casting in a fun way that requires an action setup. Which is always fun for gameplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe you can count the same effective Order Tool Yantra more than once per spell. You would also still be limited by Gnosis level number of Yantras.<br /> <br /> I'm less certain if something like a an AH Dodge, AH Brawl attack and then AH Weaponry attack would be considered three separate Order tool Yantra for a single spell (assuming the PC had all three versions of AH) or just the same one three times, and thus only counted as a single +1.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting question for the FAQ thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:26:48-07:00","id":886823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886796#post886796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't believe you can count the same effective Order Tool Yantra more than once per spell. You would also still be limited by Gnosis level number of Yantras.<br /> <br /> I'm less certain if something like a an AH Dodge, AH Brawl attack and then AH Weaponry attack would be considered three separate Order tool Yantra for a single spell (assuming the PC had all three versions of AH) or just the same one three times, and thus only counted as a single +1.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting question for the FAQ thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodging, punching, and sword swing making up 3 yantras is just too cool and really makes the extra merit purchases worth it. I think I'll allow it at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:37:57-07:00","id":886828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886823#post886823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dodging, punching, and sword swing making up 3 yantras is just too cool and really makes the extra merit purchases worth it. I think I'll allow it at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming at least a Gnosis 3+ to permit up to three Yantras for a spell, I too would be inclined to allow it as three separate and distinct Yantras, particularly since it would only provide a total +3 to the spellcasting dice pool and hardly be unbalancing. I also agree that if a player spent 6 experience for all three versions of AH and was willing to forgo casting for three turns in combat in an attempt to Dodge as well as instigate Brawl and Weaponry attacks, it would simply be cruel to not allow use of all the Yantras.<br /> <br /> However, it certainly is not above Dave to enforce canon rules that many of us would indeed define as cruel or worse. <br /> <br /> As with many other recent discussions, it would be great if Dave clarified the use of the AH merit and included it in the ultimate FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:49:06-07:00","id":887513,"title":"","content":"An interpretation of Adamant Hand my group included was that the actions involving the associated skill do not take a penalty while using Active or Focused Mage Sight. This is due to the Merit making the mundane actions into Yantras, and thus the Arrowisn't taking actions &quot;unrelated to using or perceiving magic,&quot; as the Athletics/Brawl/Melee related actions are part of their use of magic. Thus, an Arrow could carry out a fight or dodge attacks, or study a foe while chasing them, letting them be much more active and effective in Mysteries where standing around to study said Mystery in peace isn't a safe/feasible. It also means that the Arrow has better situational awareness in combat, as they can continue to dodge while watching for spells being cast so as to be ready to counter spell without facing a penalty, while other Orders would face a -2 on their dodge or other combat actions.<br /> <br /> Sure, it may be bending the rules, but it seems in character for the Arrows and thematically appropriate for those who study the Adamant Hand. It also brings the merit more in line with the benefits of the other Order Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-10-2016, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:01:03-07:00","id":887525,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's bending the rules at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:04:25-07:00","id":887530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=887525#post887525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's bending the rules at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> One of my players thought that I as the ST and the other players were playing rule lawyers, and missing the spirit of the merit/Mage sight rules by allowing the interpretation (hence my qualifier.) I just figured I would acknowledge that it was our groups interpretation and could be considered going outside the RAW, or at least implying somethings that are potentially allowed/not directly forbidden.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we took it the other way and ran with it, which has seemed to work really well to make Arrows useful beyond &quot;punch, punch, explosion Knights&quot; who hang back otherwise, while still keeping them firmly within their concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:42:45-07:00","id":888052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corginaut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming#post886143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compared to, say, the Silver Ladder merit</div> </div> </div> </div> Compare, say, the Free Council merit - you get to use different Order tools, and have to spend time to arrange for Sleepers as Yantra, which is functionally meaningless because you could just use that time to chant, draw runes, or other forms of Yantra that are just as effective, if not more so. Oh, and good luck getting NPCs together with all the same focus as you and can perform in a ritual with you, especially when you can just have that 8-again from a simple Fate blessing. Honestly, I feel like Techne is nothing more than an XP sink to help fill a concept than anything worthwhile mechanically. <br /> <br /> Compare to Egregore, which I'm still fairly sure only has the fourth dot being actually something I'd ever use in game, either as a player or an ST. <br /> <br /> Compare to Masques. Okay, Masques is pretty awesome and literally pays for itself at the fifth dot. <br /> <br /> Adamantine Hand is pretty nice when all is said and done. As others have said, lots of ways to use this effectively in combat. Meanwhile, some of the other Order merits are pretty tame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T05:17:04-07:00","id":888079,"title":"","content":"Masques not only pays for itself at the fifth dot, you can keep putting 2 XP into it to get back 5 more. Sure, you can only assume 1 Mask at once, but flexibility of having so many sets of merits is probably best benefit of them all.<br /> <br /> Techne is honestly, bad. I agree. Though &quot;getting helpers to help with my merit bruh&quot; is something you take care of with Status. Requisite some Retainers. <br /> <br /> Lex Magica is good, but not as good as people think. It takes 6 (2 for lex magica, 4 to bump up Silver Ladder status to 5) merit dots for it to provide same Yantra bonus as Shadow Name 3, and even then the bonus only applies to very specific flavor of spells (Shadow Name has this drawback, but much less, as you can customize your Persona). Other bonuses are nice, but mostly for a NPC or PVP context. <br /> <br /> Egregore is a hidden gem. It's true power is the fact that you don't suffer Status penalty across the globe, so you can literally requisite anything from anywhere. If there is a item, a rote, a word, an artifact, a contact, and in general - a resource that Mysterium has access to in at least one instance across the whole world, you can borrow it. You make a phone call and ancient chinesee artifact teleports to your doors, with a note from a Mysterium expert attached to it, and with a translation to your language. And a nice ribbon too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:26:04-07:00","id":888113,"title":"","content":"Eh, until they come out with a list of artifacts and items and rotes that you need from another city, I'm not impressed with Egregore. And my group doesn't do globetrotting, so the Status bit is meh. Eregore requires specific kinds of games to make use of, which I don't have that kind of game. <br /> <br /> I agree that Lex Magica is pretty restrictive, though, only good in some situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:52:49-07:00","id":888580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886294#post886294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most Mages are by far better at fighting with Magic than fighting with physical attacks because two dots in Weaponry, a specialty, and four dots in a fighting style could instead be a Gnosis and an Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are people who <i>buy</i> those things?<br /> <br /> Why do that when you could have Mind, and just magic up those skills instead?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Mind solves all your problems - why do we even have other Arcana?</span><br /> <br /> More on track...<br /> <br /> I dunno, I see Egregore \u2022 as <i>amazing</i> if the entire Cabal has it. You can pull off a <i>pretty big</i> bonus to a spellcasting roll by calling in favors.<br /> <br /> Also, Egregore \u2022\u2022\u2022 can be <i>reasonably</i> silly due to how amazing the Informed condition is and how <i>flexible</i> your choice of what you're Informed about is. Does a local Mysterium member have an Obsession regarding Werewolves? You can grab Informed (Werewolves). Does a local member have Allies (Police)? You can grab Informed (Police). While it's not as flashy as some of the other Order merits, it's <i>excellent</i> for what it does (arguably, you can use Informed on <i>spellcasting rolls</i>. It sorta makes sense - grab Informed (Matter) from the Moros in the area, and weave a much better Imago due to being able to... consult).<br /> <br /> And I don't see why Egregore \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022's <i>stupidly good</i> benefit is something you wouldn't use. That one merit dot means that no member of the Order is ever <i>truly</i> alone.<br /> <br /> And to finish your list:<br /> <br /> Compare to Prelacies, which are absolutely bananas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:58:42-07:00","id":888585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=888580#post888580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind solves all your problems - why do we even have other Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because some other mages might also have Mind or Prime defenses, or you're dealing with very strange creatures or those lacking sufficient cognition that they are beyond the purview of Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T15:24:57-07:00","id":888612,"title":"","content":"Mind doesn't stop a Time traveller, or a Fate master with provisions set up in place of Mind Incursions.<br /> <br /> Name an Arcana, and every other Arcana has a creative answer for dealing with it. Welcome to the cold war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T18:28:00-07:00","id":891494,"title":"","content":"Want to make awesome Adamant Hand user?<br /> <br /> 1. Pick Fate 2.<br /> 2. Pick Exceptional Luck as a Rote.<br /> 3. Get yourself a badass fighting skill.<br /> 4. Get Adamant Hand in your badass fighting skill.<br /> 5. Punish fools with your Adamant Skill, and in the same round, either punish them with buffed Reflexive Exceptional Luck, or buff yourself to obscene heights using Reflexive Exceptional Luck. Or Dodge with Fate Armor on + Reflexive Exceptional Luck.<br /> 6. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9QS0q3mGPGg\" target=\"_blank\">Win.</a><br /> <br /> Adamant Hand and this spell seems like made for each other. Add a &quot;Badass&quot; Shadow Name merit and you are the archetypical kung fu Arrow. In fact, Fate Armor synergizes with this even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-15-2016, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:07:33-07:00","id":891509,"title":"","content":"Right now I'm think of Adamant Hand Mastigos Ninja.<br /> Dodge with Mind shield so it looks like you're doing the &quot;moving so fast you disappear&quot; +1 Yandra<br /> Deliver a Bow staff to the throat +2 Yandra<br /> Duck into a sweep kick +3 Yandra<br /> Crouch in three-point stance Mutter &quot;You're already dead&quot; and cast Mind Flay as a Rote with Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11776-neotoma","name":"Neotoma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:05:52-07:00","id":891539,"title":"","content":"Adamant hand comma Dodge, and space armor. Each successful Dodge results in you being able to redirect the attack with successes equal to your dog in space for the cost of one Mana. Essentially, you get to break the action economy just a little bit comma as you gain the ability to essentially attack while dodging, and it all counts as a yantra for you well not breaking up your casting. <br /> <br /> Man, I'm beginning to see why adamant hand is so scary if you really think it through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:22:42-07:00","id":891544,"title":"","content":"Yeah. And there are Fighting Styles with riding effects keyed to successful Dodge. Martial oriented Arrow can be really good at being martial oriented. And you actually have reasons to do that other than aesthetics; I very like that it provides you with a specific interesting gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T09:28:12-07:00","id":892578,"title":"","content":"You're normally allowed one reflexive yantra a turn. Does Adamat Hand effectively give you two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:13:03-07:00","id":892598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=892578#post892578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're normally allowed one reflexive yantra a turn. Does Adamat Hand effectively give you two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how it works. You first attack or dodge (based on your version of the merit). On the same turn that you make that combat action, you can reflexively make that attack into a yantra. On the second turn, you can cast a spell. On the same turn that you cast the spell, you can use your 1 reflexive yantra.<br /> <br /> Turn 1: I swing my katana at my enemy (whilst standing on a rooftop wearing a trenchcoat). I do a bunch of damage since I rule at katanas. I declare that I'm using it reflexively as an Adamant Hand order tool. +1 bonus.<br /> Turn 2: I point my petrified wood wand at at my enemy (with a dramatic flourish) and say that this counts as my normal reflexive tool use. +1 bonus. On the same turn, I cast my spell with a combined +2 yantra bonus, allowing me to unleash torrents of lightning into my dastardly foe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 05-17-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:20:35-07:00","id":892604,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T18:17:30-07:00","id":896438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=888052#post888052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Compare, say, the Free Council merit - you get to use different Order tools, and have to spend time to arrange for Sleepers as Yantra, which is functionally meaningless because you could just use that time to chant, draw runes, or other forms of Yantra that are just as effective, if not more so. Oh, and good luck getting NPCs together with all the same focus as you and can perform in a ritual with you, especially when you can just have that 8-again from a simple Fate blessing. Honestly, I feel like Techne is nothing more than an XP sink to help fill a concept than anything worthwhile mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little late to the party. Honestly, I don't think that Techne is quite as bad as it first appears. Its worst problem is a lack of versatility. You can't just use it at any time the way you can many other Yantra merits. That said, I could imagine using it to create a newer take on the Sons of Ether or Virtual Adepts. <br /> <br /> Imagine a Free Council leader of a cabal of mortal hacktivists. A sort of Awakened version of Daisy/Skye from Agents of Shield, if you will, but working more closely with her hacktivist buddies. She uses magic to pull off amazing stunts no one else can replicate, accessing systems no one realized were even networked. <br /> <br /> It has narrow usage, but such a mage could get a ton of mileage out of using hacking as a cover for Matter or Forces spells in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6731-sobran","name":"Sobran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T18:50:27-07:00","id":896450,"title":"","content":"Techne and Egregore are actually very good because Teamwork Magic is actually THE secret to big, game changing spells. Why? <br /> Because Teamwork is not an Yantra, and yet, it adds to your casting roll. This means it contributes directly to your base pool. Which is, you know, the pool that decides how many factors can you squeeze out and put to work. A starting character who fetches a group of apprentices to help with their spell can cast a spell with maximum factors similar to these of a Master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T19:01:33-07:00","id":896452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=896450#post896450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Techne and Egregore are actually very good because Teamwork Magic is actually THE secret to big, game changing spells. Why? <br /> Because Teamwork is not an Yantra, and yet, it adds to your casting roll. This means it contributes directly to your base pool. Which is, you know, the pool that decides how many factors can you squeeze out and put to work. A starting character who fetches a group of apprentices to help with their spell can cast a spell with maximum factors similar to these of a Master.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And when you combine that with 8-again... Hoo boy. I suppose that part is of limited utility in spellcasting, but I imagine there's scenarios in which it could be useful if you're trying for an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6731-sobran","name":"Sobran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:41:14-07:00","id":896555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=896450#post896450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Techne and Egregore are actually very good because Teamwork Magic is actually THE secret to big, game changing spells. Why?<br /> Because Teamwork is not an Yantra, and yet, it adds to your casting roll. This means it contributes directly to your base pool. Which is, you know, the pool that decides how many factors can you squeeze out and put to work. A starting character who fetches a group of apprentices to help with their spell can cast a spell with maximum factors similar to these of a Master.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Egregore contributes directly to your dicepool. It does however pretty much guarantee you an Exceptional success if you can get 5 participants with the Egregore merit. Kiss Withstand goodbye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:01:31-07:00","id":896564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=896555#post896555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Egregore contributes directly to your dicepool. It does however pretty much guarantee you an Exceptional success if you can get 5 participants with the Egregore merit. Kiss Withstand goodbye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each participant with at least one dot of Egregore guarantees an additional +1 to the primary caster's dice pool plus any successes rolled by the secondary casters with at least one dot of the relevant primary arcanum and rolling their full Gnosis. That's potentially a lot of extra dice to increase factors.<br /> <br /> Techne provides the 8-Again benefit, but the secondary casters still roll with all normal Arcanum restrictions and without the auto success, and must have the same Techne focus as the primary caster (although the primary mage may use appropriate Sleeper participants as a +1 Order Tool Yantra). Techne is also a two dot merit, as opposed to only one for Egregore Mysterium Arche, and thus more likely to be possessed by more Mysterium mages.<br /> <br /> Since a simple Prime 2 spell can provide an 8-Again spellcasting benefit, I certainly would prefer Egregore for my all ritual spellcasting needs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mysteriorum Arche (\u2022): In a teamwork spellcasting roll (see p.<br /> 119) in which the character is participating, she does not suffer<br /> the \u20133 penalty to contribute without the necessary Arcanum<br /> rating, and <b>adds an automatic success if a full participant.</b> All<br /> members of the ritual team must possess this Merit. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Teamwork<br /> Mages may work together towards a common goal for spellcasting.<br /> This is handled like any other action where characters combine their<br /> efforts (see \u201cTeamwork,\u201d p. 214). The mages involved<br /> in the spellcasting must all have at least one dot in the Arcanum<br /> required to cast the spell, while the leader must have the required<br /> Arcanum rating to cast it himself. If the leader knows the spell as a<br /> Praxis or Rote, the spell gains the benefits of those methods. <b>Any<br /> secondary caster who meets the Arcanum requirements rolls her<br /> own casting and adds her successes as bonus dice to the leader</b>.<br /> If a secondary caster does not meet the Arcanum requirements,<br /> she rolls Gnosis (no Arcanum) with a \u20133 penalty, and provides<br /> any successes as bonus dice to the leader. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:49:18-07:00","id":896583,"title":"","content":"My question there is, whether the secondary rollers apply the same modifiers to their dice for the spell factors invoked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:01:41-07:00","id":896590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=896583#post896583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question there is, whether the secondary rollers apply the same modifiers to their dice for the spell factors invoked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good question, and you should offer it in the FAQ thread. <br /> <br /> Dave did indicate that secondary casters benefit from Yantra bonuses, so it's quite possible they suffer factor penalties, which could easily eviscerate their dice pool compared to what could be accomplished by a much more powerful primary caster.<br /> <br /> The one guaranteed success from Egregore 1 would then appear to be all the more impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:47:53-07:00","id":896714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sobran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=896438#post896438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little late to the party. Honestly, I don't think that Techne is quite as bad as it first appears. Its worst problem is a lack of versatility. You can't just use it at any time the way you can many other Yantra merits. That said, I could imagine using it to create a newer take on the Sons of Ether or Virtual Adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can play a Son of Ether or Virtual Adapt without it easily. In fact, its kind of the default for the FC. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine a Free Council leader of a cabal of mortal hacktivists. A sort of Awakened version of Daisy/Skye from Agents of Shield, if you will, but working more closely with her hacktivist buddies. She uses magic to pull off amazing stunts no one else can replicate, accessing systems no one realized were even networked. </div> </div> </div> You don't need mortal hactivists, though. You can do all this without mortals, or with FC Sleepwalkers hacktivists. And, given the limit on Yantra use, you can actually get more bonuses from using Runes-as-coding and other forms of high speech and other tools, and it will all be <i>faster</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has narrow usage, but such a mage could get a ton of mileage out of using hacking as a cover for Matter or Forces spells in this context. </div> </div> </div> Except for the rather important detail that you can do that without the merit. Your example has nothing to do with the merit itself. <br /> <br /> Techne lets you do three things: use new Order tools, use Sleepers as Yantra as if they were a Sleepwalker, and a bonus to group rituals that share the same merit subspace. And, in order, New Order tools to fill a concept shouldn't cost XP in my opinion - that's nothing more than an XP tax for a concept, and something I find distasteful, especially when I can aproximate using non-Order tools. Worse, many areas of focus that a mage would take often have a corresponding Legacy, and you can use the Legacy Yantra instead of taking new Order tools. <br /> <br /> Using Sleepers as Yantra takes a while to arrange and, while big from a story perspective, is complete and utter crap in terms of bonuses - there are better options that are just as thematically appropriate and faster to arrange. Call up a Sleepwalker, use a Path tool, use High Speech/Runes, use Concentration, use Persona, use Legacy Yantra, locations of power, etc. Its going to be a long time before you have an open Yantra slot that doesn't have better options. Worse, the time it takes to arrange for Sleepers to assemble in any meaningful fashion means that you can't use this for anything on the fly, and never for anything obvious.<br /> <br /> Ritual magic? The only benefit is 8-again and requires gathering everyone who shares the same focus. You can gather more mages if you don't rely on the same focus and get the 8-again from an Order imbued item, or a cotorie mate. <br /> <br /> You can reproduce the effects of the merit in a more efficent manner without spending a single XP. That makes it an XP sink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:41:54-07:00","id":896753,"title":"","content":"Most of the time, magic is not supposed to be used on the fly. That's why casting an Instant spell costs Reach. So it taking time to pull a spell together isn't really a good complaint since that's part of the basic design standards of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:06:18-07:00","id":896768,"title":"","content":"Taking time to pull a spell together is good complaint because this has nothing to do with casting times, and everything to do with Sleepers having lives of their own. Need to set a ward around an dangerous area, lets say? You can cast a spell on your own. Sleepwalker allies might understand the need and take off from work early; they might very well be part of the cabal itself, and instantly available. Mages who take part in a ritual will understand the need and donate their own free time, as suggested by the Status merit. With Sleepers, you have to arrange time when everyone can meet, and these are people with families and dates and plans and day jobs that can't just take off for a pagan ritual or a last minute computer coding party. You might very well need to wait for a weekend day, which is very inconvenient.<br /> <br /> You can cast spells when you'd normally have all these people gathered - let us say a weekly BDSM party for those FC using that subculture as a focus. Or you could go to a bondage club, assuming one is nearby. If you have all the time in the world and ability to pick the location, sure, its not a problem. And you have a spell that you can work the Sleepers into as a yantra, of course. And its not too obvious, since that would fail. If you have a need to move to somewhere unsecured, or pressed for time? These are very real concerns you have to consider, and limit when and where the merit can be used. Remember that the whole purpose of the game is to go out and investigate mysteries, and often times these mysteries are <i>dangerous</i>. Sleepers will object to certain times and places because they can't understand the need, and you can't really explain it. Mages and Sleepwalkers, on the other hand, understand.<br /> <br /> Sleepers aren't resources you can move around like chess peices. Not without controlling them with magic. These are people with lives, needs and thoughts of their own, and that needs to be taken into consideration.<br /> <br /> The sheer limit on when you can arrange for Sleepers is a huge huge drawback to the merit. The fact that you can arrange for more effective Yantra (read: higher dice bonus) in shorter amounts of time makes it virtually worthless. Its very neat from a thematic standpoint, but has little practical application. At Gnosis 5, I can have 4 Yantra prepared. I can chant High Speech, use a Persona, use a Path/Order dedicated tool, and a Legacy Yantra. Each of these can give a better bonus than a Sleeper, and can be used at any point in pretty much any spell I would cast, at any point in time, at any place. There's no reason for Sleepers here. And we're talking the upper limits on what PCs generally hit in terms of Gnosis - its rare to see games hit Supernatural Tolerance 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-23-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:38:05-07:00","id":896802,"title":"","content":"Even if they're members of your cabal, anyone who isn't a Sleeper who is participating in casting a spell also have &quot;Families and dates and plans and day jobs&quot; etc. I don't think acknowledging that people have prior commitments is the strongest argument you could have pulled together. Also, you don't need specific Sleepers at all, as long as they fall under the cultural group your Techne applies to I think it's likely you'll find someone with some free time. Also, Sleepers obviously don't know Magic is happening, so by my read you're basically skimming off the ambiance they provide which means that as long as they're actively participating in the culture they don't even have to do anything specific. You also don't actually need more than 1 Sleeper so it's not like you even have to get together a lot of people, you could just be playing on the Xbox with your Sleeper buddy and using that as your Order Tool while your other Mage buddy links in with you to give the 8-again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T14:35:44-07:00","id":1457051,"title":"","content":"Necroing a bit: about the Adamant Hand Merit...<br /> I thought that MtA 1st edition orders' books were still good reference for MtA 2nd edition. The Adamant Hand as a full fledged fighting style was really cool, especially levels ***, **** and ***** (Star, Blood and Abyss, if I remember correctly), but the first 2 levels were nice as well. On the other hand the Adamant Hand merit as described in MtA 2nd edition Corebook was... eh, nice, but it lacked something. It was underwhelming.<br /> So... is the 1st edition adamant hand as a fighting style effectively dead and buried? Will it come back somehow, maybe a new future sourcebook on orders and something special, more detailed, for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T22:58:56-07:00","id":1457079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457051#post1457051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necroing a bit: about the Adamant Hand Merit...<br /> I thought that MtA 1st edition orders' books were still good reference for MtA 2nd edition. The Adamant Hand as a full fledged fighting style was really cool, especially levels ***, **** and ***** (Star, Blood and Abyss, if I remember correctly), but the first 2 levels were nice as well. On the other hand the Adamant Hand merit as described in MtA 2nd edition Corebook was... eh, nice, but it lacked something. It was underwhelming.<br /> So... is the 1st edition adamant hand as a fighting style effectively dead and buried? Will it come back somehow, maybe a new future sourcebook on orders and something special, more detailed, for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant Hand can be very powerful, especially with the new addition of the firearms branch in Nameless &amp; Accursed.<br /> <br /> The way I understand it is that you can make use of that skill in combat and a spell on the same turn. So it means you can be dodging a werewolf or doing complex parkour in a chase while casting at the same time. You can lay covering fire and hit the enemy's position with an AoE in the same turn. You could throw a dagger at one foe and a spell at the other. That is huge, it increases the mage's combat options in a major way. Adamant Hand makes the Arrows terrifying because they become so much more efficient on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> Not only that, you choose when to use the bonus and there is no upper limit to the maximum. So in an engagement that lasts a bit, they could accumulate something like a +6 reflexive yantra to use on a really powerful spell, maybe even to teleport away from the danger.<br /> <br /> Regarding adapting the 1ed version, perhaps a Legacy could be a way to approach it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-18-2021, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T23:14:09-07:00","id":1457080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457079#post1457079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I understand it is that you can make use of that skill in combat and a spell on the same turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>A two-dot Merit does not allow you to break the action economy in this fashion. You can make use of that Skill and <i>prepare</i> a spell, but casting is still an instant action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not only that, you choose when to use the bonus and there is no upper limit to the maximum. </div> </div> </div>There is the same upper limit that exists for every Yantra, which is the one on the Gnosis chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T05:15:28-07:00","id":1457094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457080#post1457080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A two-dot Merit does not allow you to break the action economy in this fashion. You can make use of that Skill and <i>prepare</i> a spell, but casting is still an instant action.<br /> <br /> There is the same upper limit that exists for every Yantra, which is the one on the Gnosis chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, does that mean each +1 counts as its own separate yantra ? I thought it counted as a single one that accumulates value until you use it.<br /> <br /> If that is the case, then its extremely underwhelming. I thought the objective of the merit was to incentivize the diversity of combat approaches when spellcasting is heavily favored. Which it does, but not in a way that is as eminently useful or flavorful as other Order merits. Perhaps I am missing something about its potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T05:57:05-07:00","id":1457098,"title":"","content":"The purpose of 2e Adamant Hand is merely to give access to an additional Order Tool Yantra (in addition to the Order Tool Yantra everyone in an Order already gains access to) for Adamantine Arrow, much like Techn\u00e9 for Free Council, Lex Magica for Silver Ladder and the second dot of Prelacy for Seers of the Throne. (Mysterium instead gets their own Mystery Cult Initiation Merit in the form of Egregore, and Guardians of the Veil get their cool Masques.)<br /> <br /> What Adamant Hand does, is that when you make an attack, that attack can be used as a reflexive Order Tool Yantra. Order Tool Yantras only grant +1.<br /> Edit: You still need to spend the usual action to cast the spell once all Yantras have been added. Generally it's an instant action (which can definitely not be taken during the same turn as the combat action) but reflexive spells can still be cast the same turn.<br /> <br /> In comparison to Techn\u00e9 and Lex Magica, I have to agree that it's lackluster. In combat, you do get one additional die on whatever spell you'd like to cast (since you'll never fill out all the Yantra slots during a combat scene) but only if you engage in physical combat first (either attacking or Dodging). It's a nice thing to have when it becomes relevant, but it's doubtful it'll be relevant often enough to justify its cost. You can't use it on pre-combat buffs, and in my experience you generally don't mix spells and attacks during combat since situations tends to favour one approach over the other.<br /> Techn\u00e9 has the problem that +1 Yantras are already easily available outside of combat (if you have any Yantra slots over for Yantras that don't grant 2 or more dice), but in an all Free Council cabal it could be somewhat potent since it can grant 8-Again on ritual casts (which increases the chance of Exceptional Success, but unfortunately not the chance of succeeding in the first place).<br /> Lex Magica, on the other hand, is fucking gold compared to either. On top of giving some really good advantages outside of magic (which neither Adamant Hand nor Techn\u00e9 does), the Yantra part can be increase to a maximum of +3 which is a huge deal. Even if you'd remove the non-Yantra advantages and only have three dots of Order/Consilium Status (which makes it a +2 Yantra), it's still better than both Adamant Hand and Techn\u00e9, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-18-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T11:31:20-07:00","id":1457117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457080#post1457080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A two-dot Merit does not allow you to break the action economy in this fashion. You can make use of that Skill and <i>prepare</i> a spell, but casting is still an instant action.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant: in 1st edition Mage, one could physically attack *and* cast a spell using the Adamant Hand technique &quot;Star&quot;. To do so:<br /> - A Mage had to learn the 1st and 2nd fighting style merit, before being able to learn the Star (3rd fighting style merit). XPs had to be expended.<br /> - A Mage had to learn and pay this fighting style separately for each Arcanum.<br /> - A Mage had to spend 1 willpower point for every single use of the Star.<br /> - A Mage had to keep following the Adamantine Arrow philosophy or lose all benefits from this fighting style.<br /> <br /> I guess these 4 rules put together were enough for the developers to decide to allow an action economy exception?<br /> Plus the mental picture of a mage, hitting hard with a punch and at the same time releasing magical power in a spell, is just too cool to just shelve away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T16:41:50-07:00","id":1457157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457117#post1457117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the mental picture of a mage, hitting hard with a punch and at the same time releasing magical power in a spell, is just too cool to just shelve away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the boring-but-practical method to do that would be just casting the spell at Touch range. If a mage who can deliver Thunderbolts with his palms says it\u2019s stylish, it\u2019s <i>stylish</i>.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps allow Aimed Spells to be \u2018thrown\u2019 at point-blank range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T01:11:20-07:00","id":1457191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457157#post1457157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the boring-but-practical method to do that would be just casting the spell at Touch range. If a mage who can deliver Thunderbolts with his palms says it\u2019s stylish, it\u2019s <i>stylish</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, you can't in second edition. Touching an opponent in combat is a type of attack action which is always an instant action so you wouldn't be able to both do that and cast a spell (unless it's a reflexive spell). And even if you could, you wouldn't deal any damage from the attack which defeats half the purpose of such a combo (the other half being that it's stylish).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T01:24:09-07:00","id":1457193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457191#post1457191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, you can't in second edition. Touching an opponent in combat is a type of attack action which is always an instant action so you wouldn't be able to both do that and cast a spell (unless it's a reflexive spell). And even if you could, you wouldn't deal any damage from the attack which defeats half the purpose of such a combo</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Thought I nailed it. Guess I need to reread those parts<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (the other half being that it's stylish). </div> </div> </div>Hey, at least that\u2019s working lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T11:16:10-07:00","id":1457217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=1457191#post1457191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, you can't in second edition. Touching an opponent in combat is a type of attack action which is always an instant action so you wouldn't be able to both do that and cast a spell (unless it's a reflexive spell). And even if you could, you wouldn't deal any damage from the attack which defeats half the purpose of such a combo (the other half being that it's stylish).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anyone else on the forums who tried putting together a houserule for old-style adamant hand attacks or even just for 1 turn touch-range spell on enemies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}